Team,

Before this becomes another standing report, can we answer the real question?

Product needs to define successful channel adoption as sustained useful activ=
ity rather than enrolment or one event. The possible stories are that adoptio=
n differs by product and customer need, that first successful use predicts co=
ntinued use, or that customers return to assisted channels after failure.

This has returned because the previous answer was useful but not strong enoug=
h to become a standing rule. Use August 2021 as the new evidence point rather=
 than recycling the earlier conclusion. Several teams are reporting more fail=
ed or retried activity than they expected, but they do not agree on the cause.

Please prepare a model-ready table, data dictionary and an honest baseline. T=
he output must help us decide which onboarding journey and success metric sho=
uld change.

Data available: monthly account snapshots, status events, limits, product enr=
olments and signatories; transaction-level timestamps, channels, amounts, sta=
tuses and error context; customer contacts, complaints and suggestions; ATM a=
ttempts, host responses, PIN attempts, blocked-card state and latency.

Please state the limitation plainly: Available data supports channel behaviou=
r but not every app screen, click or abandoned session.

Thanks
